> It looks like there’s an issue with the way the links are being created in the Shiny `nav_menu()`. The `tags$a()` function seems to be missing the `href` keyword argument, which is necessary for creating a hyperlink. Here's how you can properly format your `nav_menu()` function:
> 
> ```r
> nav_menu(
>   title = "Links",
>   align = "right",
>   nav_item(tags$a(href = "https://www.accreu.eu/", "ACCREU")),
>   nav_item(tags$a(href = "https://www.lse.ac.uk/granthaminstitute/projects/attenuate-creating-the-enabling-conditions-for-uk-climate-adaptation-investment/", "ATTENUATE"))
> )
> ```
> 
> By specifically using the `href` attribute within `tags$a()`, you ensure that the titles appear as clickable links directing users to the specified URLs. This should resolve the issue and display them as functioning hyperlinks on your Shiny page.
**user**:
> Also, how do I include a link to a local (within the shiny app folder) PDF?
**assistant**:
> To include a link to a local PDF file within your Shiny app, you can use the `tags$a()` function to create the hyperlink. You simply need to specify the relative path to the PDF file in your app's directory. Here's an example:
> 
> Assuming your PDF file is named `document.pdf` and is located in a folder named `www` (which is the conventional directory for static files in Shiny apps), you could set it up like this:
> 
> ```r
> nav_menu(
>   title = "Links",
>   align = "right",
>   nav_item(tags$a(href = "https://www.accreu.eu/", "ACCREU")),
>   nav_item(tags$a(href = "https://www.lse.ac.uk/granthaminstitute/projects/attenuate-creating-the-enabling-conditions-for-uk-climate-adaptation-investment/", "ATTENUATE")),
>   nav_item(tags$a(href = "www/document.pdf", "Download PDF"))
> )
> ```
> 
> ### Ensure the Following:
> 1. **File Structure**: Place your `document.pdf` file in the `www` folder of your Shiny app.
> 2. **App Deployment**: If you deploy your app (e.g., on shinyapps.io), the `www` folder and its contents will be uploaded automatically.
> 
> ### Note:
> - The link above (`www/document.pdf`) is relative. If your PDF is not in the `www` folder, adjust the path accordingly.
> - To open the PDF in the same tab, the default behavior is to load it directly. To open in a new tab, you can add `target = "_blank"` to the `tags$a()` like this:
> 
> ```r
> nav_item(tags$a(href = "www/document.pdf", "Download PDF", target = "_blank"))
> ```
> 
> This should provide a working link to your local PDF within your Shiny application!
